  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Mill & Mine in Knoxville, Tennessee, on August 9, 2024, delivering a 100-minute set that serves as the only available recording of this event [1]. The lineup featured Peter Hughes, who was unexpectedly out with COVID, leading to a duo configuration for much of the show [1]. However, Ben, the band’s audio engineer, contributed vocals on select tracks, a substitution clearly audible in the audio [1]. The band also acknowledged support from Field Medic, whose performance that same night is available on the Internet Archive [1]. The setlist opened with the rare “The Legend of Chavo Guerrero” and included “Water Tower” and “Incandescent Ruins” [1]. A notable highlight was “Tulsa Imperative,” a bustout appearing for the first time in 194 archived shows, marking a 2,841-day gap [1]. Other tracks included “In Memory of Satan,” “Fresh Tattoo,” and “Dutch Orchestra Blues” [1]. The performance concluded with an encore containing “You or Your Memory,” “Woke Up New,” “Waylon Jennings Live!,” and “No Children” [1]. The recording is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, taped and transferred by LMGBTapes [1]. This show is number 424 of 467 in the archive’s collection for the performer [2]. A poster for the event is credited to panetory.com [3].",
